NOTICE
======

Iris for Windows is the desktop assistant for publik (publikhq.com) — a
text-first companion that lives in the system tray. You type a question, it
answers with the context of what is on your screen, and it can fly a small
cursor to point at the UI element it is talking about. It also opens publik's
install guides from `iris://guide/...` links.

Iris for Windows is a fork of clicky-windows by tekram
(https://github.com/tekram/clicky-windows), which is itself a Windows port of
Clicky by Farza (https://github.com/farzaa/clicky). Both are licensed under the
MIT License. The upstream MIT license text is preserved in this directory as
LICENSE.upstream, and that license continues to apply to the portions of this
codebase derived from either project.

Changes in this fork:
- Voice features were removed: AssemblyAI / OpenAI / local-Whisper
  transcription, ElevenLabs / OpenAI / Windows-SAPI text-to-speech, audio
  capture, and push-to-talk. Iris is text-first.
- The OpenAI and OpenRouter chat providers were removed. Iris is
  Anthropic-only, reached over exactly two transports (see README.md).
- The BYOK-plaintext-JSON settings store was replaced with Electron
  `safeStorage` (DPAPI) for every secret.
- publik integration was added: a funded assistant transport behind Supabase
  sign-in, `iris://` deep links, publik install guides, and a canonical
  external-host allowlist.
- The app was rebranded from Clicky to Iris.

Based on clicky-windows by tekram (MIT), and on Clicky by Farza (MIT).
